/T (  3.2 Traffic Prediction  Traffic Prediction refers to the process of forecasting future network traffic behavior, such as bandwidth usage, packet counts, or data rates, based on past measurements. It plays a crucial role in network planning, congestion control, and anomaly detection, allowing systems to adapt proactively rather than reactively. Inputs typically include historical traffic data, time features \(like hour or weekday\), and sometimes external variables such as service load or weather conditions [Zha22]. )
/E (  3.2 Traffic Prediction  Traffic Prediction refers to the process of forecasting future network traffic behavior, such as bandwidth usage, packet counts, or data rates, based on past measurements. It plays a crucial role in network planning, congestion control, and anomaly detection, allowing systems to adapt proactively rather than reactively. Inputs typically include historical traffic data, time features \(like hour or weekday\), and sometimes external variables such as service load or weather conditions [Zha22]. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1029 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 419 0 R
/T (3.3 Long Short-Term Memory Model  Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) is a type of Recurrent Neural Network \(RNN\) built to handle sequential data, like time-series, speech, or text. It overcomes the vanishing gradient problem common in standard RNNs, which struggles to remember information from many steps earlier in  a sequence [Gre17]. )
/E (3.3 Long Short-Term Memory Model  Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) is a type of Recurrent Neural Network \(RNN\) built to handle sequential data, like time-series, speech, or text. It overcomes the vanishing gradient problem common in standard RNNs, which struggles to remember information from many steps earlier in  a sequence [Gre17]. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
