/P 419 0 R
/T (To understand how LSTM works, it is important to look at its architecture. Each unit has a specific structure made of a memory cell and three gates that control the flow of information. These elements help the network decide what to keep, what to update, and what to pass forward, )
/E (To understand how LSTM works, it is important to look at its architecture. Each unit has a specific structure made of a memory cell and three gates that control the flow of information. These elements help the network decide what to keep, what to update, and what to pass forward, )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1032 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 419 0 R
/T (A traditional approach used in time-series forecasting is the Auto Regressive Integrated Moving Average \(ARIMA\) model, which combines autoregression and moving averages with differencing to handle trends. While ARIMA performs well on data with linear patterns and stationary behavior, its accuracy declines in complex, noisy environments like network traffic, where non-linearities are common. )
/E (A traditional approach used in time-series forecasting is the Auto Regressive Integrated Moving Average \(ARIMA\) model, which combines autoregression and moving averages with differencing to handle trends. While ARIMA performs well on data with linear patterns and stationary behavior, its accuracy declines in complex, noisy environments like network traffic, where non-linearities are common. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1033 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 419 0 R
/T (Support Vector Regression \(SVR\) is another method frequently applied to traffic forecasting. It can model non-linear relationships using kernel functions and has shown solid performance in short-term prediction tasks. However, it still requires careful manual feature selection and struggles with long-term dependencies [Lyp24]. )
/E (Support Vector Regression \(SVR\) is another method frequently applied to traffic forecasting. It can model non-linear relationships using kernel functions and has shown solid performance in short-term prediction tasks. However, it still requires careful manual feature selection and struggles with long-term dependencies [Lyp24]. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1034 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 419 0 R
/T (In contrast, LSTM networks are designed to handle sequences with long-term patterns, making them especially suitable for traffic prediction. LSTM models can automatically learn from raw time-series data using internal memory cells and gates to capture both short-term fluctuations and long-term trends. Studies like [Zha22] have demonstrated that LSTM significantly outperforms ARIMA and SVR in terms of prediction accuracy, especially when evaluated using common metrics such as Root Mean Square Error \(RMSE\), Mean Absolute Error \(MAE\), and Mean Absolute Percentage Error \(MAPE\). )
/E (In contrast, LSTM networks are designed to handle sequences with long-term patterns, making them especially suitable for traffic prediction. LSTM models can automatically learn from raw time-series data using internal memory cells and gates to capture both short-term fluctuations and long-term trends. Studies like [Zha22] have demonstrated that LSTM significantly outperforms ARIMA and SVR in terms of prediction accuracy, especially when evaluated using common metrics such as Root Mean Square Error \(RMSE\), Mean Absolute Error \(MAE\), and Mean Absolute Percentage Error \(MAPE\). )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1035 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 419 0 R
/T (Because of their ability to model complex temporal relationships without manually selected featuress, LSTM-based models have become the preferred choice in many modern traffic forecasting systems. Their scalability and robustness make them well-suited for both real-time applications and large-scale deployments [Zha22]. )
/E (Because of their ability to model complex temporal relationships without manually selected featuress, LSTM-based models have become the preferred choice in many modern traffic forecasting systems. Their scalability and robustness make them well-suited for both real-time applications and large-scale deployments [Zha22]. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
