/E (In any system that includes multiple services, containers, or simulated network topologies, it becomes very important to monitor what is happening at every moment. Monitoring tools allow us to collect useful data about system performance, network usage, system health, and application activity. In this thesis, three popular and open-source tools were used to build a complete monitoring setup: Prometheus, Grafana, and Pushgateway. These tools work together to collect, store, and display information in a way that helps us understand the behavior of the system over time [Pro25]. This is very useful when testing and simulating network topologies )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
