/P 427 0 R
/T (Each metric collected is associated with a timestamp and a set of descriptive labels \(such as instance, job, or device\) to enable precise filtering and identification. The collection process is fully automated and centralized, following a pull-based model in which Prometheus initiates data retrieval from each desired endpoint. What makes Prometheus very useful is its query language, PromQL, which allows users to extract and process metrics in real time. With PromQL, we can calculate averages, detect changes over time, compare values across devices, and much more [Pro25]. This architecture allows Prometheus to maintain complete control over the frequency, scope, and organization of the monitoring process. Its ability to address targets directly via IP and port makes it well-suited for containerized environments, simulated network topologies, or distributed systems where services may run isolated and have access to the Internet [Pou24a]. )
/E (Each metric collected is associated with a timestamp and a set of descriptive labels \(such as instance, job, or device\) to enable precise filtering and identification. The collection process is fully automated and centralized, following a pull-based model in which Prometheus initiates data retrieval from each desired endpoint. What makes Prometheus very useful is its query language, PromQL, which allows users to extract and process metrics in real time. With PromQL, we can calculate averages, detect changes over time, compare values across devices, and much more [Pro25]. This architecture allows Prometheus to maintain complete control over the frequency, scope, and organization of the monitoring process. Its ability to address targets directly via IP and port makes it well-suited for containerized environments, simulated network topologies, or distributed systems where services may run isolated and have access to the Internet [Pou24a]. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 427 0 R
/T (Figure 3 presents the user interface of Prometheus, showing both the query entry page and the target status page. For example, a common query might be for the metric ifHCOutOctets, which shows how much outgoing network traffic was transmitted through a specific interface. The result displays a list of current values for each target \(which could be a container, a virtual machine, or another monitored device\). Each entry includes labels that help identify where the data is coming from, such as the name of the interface or the IP address of the instance. The tool also supports filtering and mathematical operations to allow more advanced analysis. This is helpful for detecting unusual patterns, slowdowns, or failures in the system. In addition to the query interface, the second panel displays the target status view, where users can see which endpoints are currently reachable, the health of each target, and when data was last successfully scraped. This allows for real-time infrastructure monitoring and quick identification of connectivity or availability issues. Together, these interface elements provide both high-level visibility and low-level control over the monitored environment. )
/E (Figure 3 presents the user interface of Prometheus, showing both the query entry page and the target status page. For example, a common query might be for the metric ifHCOutOctets, which shows how much outgoing network traffic was transmitted through a specific interface. The result displays a list of current values for each target \(which could be a container, a virtual machine, or another monitored device\). Each entry includes labels that help identify where the data is coming from, such as the name of the interface or the IP address of the instance. The tool also supports filtering and mathematical operations to allow more advanced analysis. This is helpful for detecting unusual patterns, slowdowns, or failures in the system. In addition to the query interface, the second panel displays the target status view, where users can see which endpoints are currently reachable, the health of each target, and when data was last successfully scraped. This allows for real-time infrastructure monitoring and quick identification of connectivity or availability issues. Together, these interface elements provide both high-level visibility and low-level control over the monitored environment. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
