/T (Node Exporter - is used to monitor Linux system-level metrics such as CPU usage, memory, disk I/O, network statistics, and file system activity. It runs as a background service directly on the machine being monitored and exposes metrics at an HTTP endpoint, usually on port 9100 [Pro25]. When Prometheus scrapes the Node Exporter, it retrieves hundreds of metrics formatted as plain )
/E (Node Exporter - is used to monitor Linux system-level metrics such as CPU usage, memory, disk I/O, network statistics, and file system activity. It runs as a background service directly on the machine being monitored and exposes metrics at an HTTP endpoint, usually on port 9100 [Pro25]. When Prometheus scrapes the Node Exporter, it retrieves hundreds of metrics formatted as plain )
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [10]
>>
