/T (Idle container - this container represents a device that is powered on, but it does not send or receive data. It behaves like a desktop computer or server that is running in the background, without user activity. It is important because many real systems do not constantly generate traffic. The container allows comparison between an idle state and more active or suspicious behaviors. )
/E (Idle container - this container represents a device that is powered on, but it does not send or receive data. It behaves like a desktop computer or server that is running in the background, without user activity. It is important because many real systems do not constantly generate traffic. The container allows comparison between an idle state and more active or suspicious behaviors. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [11]
>>
