/S /H1
/P 433 0 R
/T ( Ping container - this container regularly sends ICMP echo requests, which are also known as "ping" packets. It mimics a device or script that checks if other systems are reachable on the network. These pings are sent at fixed intervals and help simulate simple connectivity tests. It is useful for scenarios where devices need to check the status of other devices, like in automated monitoring or alerting systems. )
/E ( Ping container - this container regularly sends ICMP echo requests, which are also known as "ping" packets. It mimics a device or script that checks if other systems are reachable on the network. These pings are sent at fixed intervals and help simulate simple connectivity tests. It is useful for scenarios where devices need to check the status of other devices, like in automated monitoring or alerting systems. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
