<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 433 0 R
/T ( TCP-HTTP container - this container generates standard TCP traffic by sending repeated HTTP requests to a specified address. It simulates a user browsing web pages or a background process communicating with a web server. This type of activity is very common in real networks and helps create a realistic traffic pattern. The container shows how regular web traffic looks. )
/E ( TCP-HTTP container - this container generates standard TCP traffic by sending repeated HTTP requests to a specified address. It simulates a user browsing web pages or a background process communicating with a web server. This type of activity is very common in real networks and helps create a realistic traffic pattern. The container shows how regular web traffic looks. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [15]
>>
