1292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 433 0 R
/T ( Anomaly container - this container is designed to produce unusual or irregular traffic, simulating possible network problems or malicious behavior. It primarily uses the ping command, but unlike the normal Ping container, it sends packets at random intervals or in short bursts. This creates an abnormal pattern that stands out from the rest. Additionally, tools like curl can be used inside the container to send strange or repetitive HTTP requests, such as accessing rarely used endpoints or sending malformed data. )
/E ( Anomaly container - this container is designed to produce unusual or irregular traffic, simulating possible network problems or malicious behavior. It primarily uses the ping command, but unlike the normal Ping container, it sends packets at random intervals or in short bursts. This creates an abnormal pattern that stands out from the rest. Additionally, tools like curl can be used inside the container to send strange or repetitive HTTP requests, such as accessing rarely used endpoints or sending malformed data. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
