/T (  The interface GigabitEthernet2/0 command selects the interface on the. In this setup, the GigabitEthernet2/0 interface is used to create a link between the virtual router from GNS3 and the Cloud node. The Cloud node acts as a bridge that connects the GNS3 topology to the real physical network - a router in this thesis. This connection is important because it allows the Docker containers inside GNS3 to have Internet access and be accessible from outside the network for metric collection. )
/E (  The interface GigabitEthernet2/0 command selects the interface on the. In this setup, the GigabitEthernet2/0 interface is used to create a link between the virtual router from GNS3 and the Cloud node. The Cloud node acts as a bridge that connects the GNS3 topology to the real physical network - a router in this thesis. This connection is important because it allows the Docker containers inside GNS3 to have Internet access and be accessible from outside the network for metric collection. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
