/T (The ip nat outside command is used to define this interface as the external or "outside" side of the NAT configuration. This is important because the router needs to know which interface handles traffic going or coming from outside the GNS3 virtual network. NAT allows devices inside the GNS3 topology, like Docker containers, to be accessed from outside using external IP and specific ports. )
/E (The ip nat outside command is used to define this interface as the external or "outside" side of the NAT configuration. This is important because the router needs to know which interface handles traffic going or coming from outside the GNS3 virtual network. NAT allows devices inside the GNS3 topology, like Docker containers, to be accessed from outside using external IP and specific ports. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [12]
