/P 435 0 R
/T (As the main data collector, Prometheus manages all incoming data before being visualized or analyzed. It works by periodically sending HTTP requests \(called scrapes\) to endpoints that expose metrics in a specific format. In this thesis, Prometheus collects data from two types of endpoints: Docker containers \(via Node Exporter\) and Cisco Router \(via SNMP\). This integration is achieved by specifying the endpoints \(targets\) in the Prometheus configuration file \(prometheus.yml\). Below is a snippet of the Prometheus configuration file used, written in YAML format. It defines how Prometheus collects metrics from Docker containers, the Pushgateway, and the Cisco router in the GNS3 topology:  global: )
/E (As the main data collector, Prometheus manages all incoming data before being visualized or analyzed. It works by periodically sending HTTP requests \(called scrapes\) to endpoints that expose metrics in a specific format. In this thesis, Prometheus collects data from two types of endpoints: Docker containers \(via Node Exporter\) and Cisco Router \(via SNMP\). This integration is achieved by specifying the endpoints \(targets\) in the Prometheus configuration file \(prometheus.yml\). Below is a snippet of the Prometheus configuration file used, written in YAML format. It defines how Prometheus collects metrics from Docker containers, the Pushgateway, and the Cisco router in the GNS3 topology:  global: )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [10]
>>
