/T (  This configuration defines a metric called ifInOctets, which counts the total number of bytes received on a network interface. OID is the SNMP identifier for this specific data. The metric is of type counter, meaning it only increases over time. The indexes section tells Prometheus how to identify which interface each metric value belongs to, using ifIndex as a label. The lookups section links the numeric interface index to human-readable labels like ifAlias, ifDescr, and ifName, which provide more detailed descriptions of each interface. These SNMP metrics can be accessed through a web browser at address: http://localhost:9116. Each metric is displayed with detailed labels for every interface on the router. For example, the ifInOctets metric shows how many bytes have been received on each network interface. A sample result returned by SNMP Exporter, showing the ifInOctets values for two interfaces \(Fa0/0 and Gi2/0\) on the router:  ifInOctets{ifAlias="",ifDescr="Fa0/0",ifIndex="1",ifName="Fa0/0"} 567247 ifInOctets{ifAlias="",ifDescr="Gi2/0",ifIndex="6",ifName="Gi2/0"} 256082  )
/E (  This configuration defines a metric called ifInOctets, which counts the total number of bytes received on a network interface. OID is the SNMP identifier for this specific data. The metric is of type counter, meaning it only increases over time. The indexes section tells Prometheus how to identify which interface each metric value belongs to, using ifIndex as a label. The lookups section links the numeric interface index to human-readable labels like ifAlias, ifDescr, and ifName, which provide more detailed descriptions of each interface. These SNMP metrics can be accessed through a web browser at address: http://localhost:9116. Each metric is displayed with detailed labels for every interface on the router. For example, the ifInOctets metric shows how many bytes have been received on each network interface. A sample result returned by SNMP Exporter, showing the ifInOctets values for two interfaces \(Fa0/0 and Gi2/0\) on the router:  ifInOctets{ifAlias="",ifDescr="Fa0/0",ifIndex="1",ifName="Fa0/0"} 567247 ifInOctets{ifAlias="",ifDescr="Gi2/0",ifIndex="6",ifName="Gi2/0"} 256082  )
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
