/T (Each metric's DataFrame is appended to a list \(dfs\). After processing all the metrics, the function combines all the individual DataFrames into one final DataFrame \(df_final\). The merger is done using the timestamp column, so that all metric values are aligned by time. It keeps only the rows where all metrics have valid data, removing any rows with missing values. The final DataFrame is sorted by timestamp to ensure chronological order. )
/E (Each metric's DataFrame is appended to a list \(dfs\). After processing all the metrics, the function combines all the individual DataFrames into one final DataFrame \(df_final\). The merger is done using the timestamp column, so that all metric values are aligned by time. It keeps only the rows where all metrics have valid data, removing any rows with missing values. The final DataFrame is sorted by timestamp to ensure chronological order. )
