/T (After the input data has been prepared and turned into sequences, it needs to be reshaped into a format that the LSTM model can understand. Specifically, the LSTM expects the data to have three dimensions: \(number of samples, time steps, number of features\). Reshaping step is necessary for Keras LSTM layers [Cal22]. This helps the model learn how traffic values change over time, by looking at patterns in the previous steps:  X = X.reshape\(\(X.shape[0], X.shape[1], X.shape[2]\)\) )
