/T (Next, the script defines and trains a simple LSTM model. The model has one LSTM layer with 32 units, which learns patterns in the time series data, followed by a dense layer with one output, which predicts the next traffic value. The model is compiled using the Adam optimizer and Mean Squared Error \(MSE\) as the loss function and then, trained for 5 epochs. Using Adam optimizer with MSE loss is a common and effective approach in training regression models on time series data [Gre17; Cal22]:  model = tf.keras.models.Sequential\([ )
