/T (  Once training is complete, the model makes a prediction for the last point in the dataset. Both the predicted and the true values are still scaled between 0 and 1, so they need to be converted back to their original scale using the same MinMax scaler. Only the value of ifHCInOctets \(incoming traffic\) is predicted. The inverse transformation restores the values to their real scale for easy comparison with real network traffic volumes [Lyp24], [Sal24].  y_pred_scaled = model.predict\(X[-1].reshape\(1, X.shape[1], X.shape[2]\)\) true_value_scaled = y[-1]  dummy = np.zeros\(\(1, len\(metrics\)\)\)  dummy[0][0] = y_pred_scaled[0][0]  predicted_value = scaler.inverse_transform\(dummy\)[0][0]  dummy[0][0] = true_value_scaled  true_value = scaler.inverse_transform\(dummy\)[0][0]  prediction_timestamp = df["timestamp"].iloc[-1]   )
/E (  Once training is complete, the model makes a prediction for the last point in the dataset. Both the predicted and the true values are still scaled between 0 and 1, so they need to be converted back to their original scale using the same MinMax scaler. Only the value of ifHCInOctets \(incoming traffic\) is predicted. The inverse transformation restores the values to their real scale for easy comparison with real network traffic volumes [Lyp24], [Sal24].  y_pred_scaled = model.predict\(X[-1].reshape\(1, X.shape[1], X.shape[2]\)\) true_value_scaled = y[-1]  dummy = np.zeros\(\(1, len\(metrics\)\)\)  dummy[0][0] = y_pred_scaled[0][0]  predicted_value = scaler.inverse_transform\(dummy\)[0][0]  dummy[0][0] = true_value_scaled  true_value = scaler.inverse_transform\(dummy\)[0][0]  prediction_timestamp = df["timestamp"].iloc[-1]   )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
