/T (One example of such a result is shown in Figure 15, where a Prometheus query \(rate\(ifHcOutOctets[5m]\)\) displays the outgoing traffic on all interfaces of the router. These metrics are collected using SNMP \(running on router\). Only two interfaces have visible traffic, while the others show a value of 0. This happens because FastEthernet0/0 is connected to the  containers, where most of the local communication happens, and GigabitEthernet2/0 is the  interface connected to the Cloud node, which provides Internet access, so, all the traffic going outside the GNS3 network passes through this interface. )
