/T (  is not enough for the model to fully learn the traffic patterns, and, as a result, its predictions are less accurate in the first few minutes. However, after around 10 minutes of running, the model begins to recognize the pattern better, and the predicted values start to follow the real traffic. This can be observed in the graph in Figure 17, where after the initial learning period from the beggining, the two lines \(real and predicted traffic\) almost overlap. So, the delay and differences at the beginning are normal due to limited data and the model improves quickly after more data becomes available. )
/E (  is not enough for the model to fully learn the traffic patterns, and, as a result, its predictions are less accurate in the first few minutes. However, after around 10 minutes of running, the model begins to recognize the pattern better, and the predicted values start to follow the real traffic. This can be observed in the graph in Figure 17, where after the initial learning period from the beggining, the two lines \(real and predicted traffic\) almost overlap. So, the delay and differences at the beginning are normal due to limited data and the model improves quickly after more data becomes available. )
/Pg 66 0 R
