endobj
1901 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (The main goal of this thesis was to build a complete system that can monitor and analyze traffic in any network that uses a router, working even without an Internet connection, but this includes some limitations. The system was designed to collect data in real time and visualize them to understand the current state, helping to track the traffic, to check the device activity, and to detect issues earlier. By using this system, it became much easier to manage network resources and to detect if some problems occur. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1902 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (Another important part of this thesis was the integration of AI components to the system so that we do not just observe the network. Artificial Intelligence added two main features: \(1\) detection of anomalies in the network; and \(2\) prediction of future traffic. The first helps to find strange or unusual activity caused by errors, misconfigurations, or security threats. The second one helps to anticipate problems before they appear, such as congestion or system overload. These functions give more time to react and to prevent issues that can affect network performance. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1903 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (This monitoring system was built using only open-source tools because they were free and easy to integrate. Another important reason is the large community support for these tools, which contributes to solving the problems quickly and improving the system over time. Also, they are flexible and customizable, allowing them to be adapted for different network purposes. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1904 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (Currently, there are some commercial solutions on the market, such as SolarWinds, PRTG, or Datadog, similar to ours. However, they cost money, they have usage limits, or they are not fully customizable. Unlike those, the thesis proposed a solution fully transparent, easy to modify, and does not rely on cloud or paid services. It also includes AI-based processing, which is usually not available in the standard monitoring tools without additional costs. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1905 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (Future improvements of this thesis can focus on both the AI part and the network configuration. The current LSTM model is trained from scratch every time using only 10 minutes of data, limiting the accuracy of traffic prediction, so, a better approach would be to train the model on more data, save it, and update it over time. Also, more advanced models or longer training sequences could improve results. For anomaly detection, adjusting the contamination level or combining different models might reduce false alerts. On the network side, the topology can also be extended by adding new devices that generate more and different types of traffic, such as DNS, file transfers, or video streams, testing the system under more realistic conditions. Another option is to test other AI models \(like GRU, CNN, or Random Forest\) and compare their performance with the current used models, to understand which is more suitable for real-time traffic prediction or anomaly detection in this type of network. On the network side, the GNS3 topology can be expanded by adding new types of devices, such as DNS servers, file transfer nodes, or media streaming containers, to simulate a wider range of real-world traffic. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1906 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (Generative AI tools were used to improve the clarity and readability of the text. Specifically, it was applied in sections such as Theoretical Fundamentals and Implementation for rephrasing, polishing, and enhancing expression. All content was carefully reviewed to ensure accuracy and originality. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
