/Title (In contrast, LSTM networks are designed to handle sequences with long-term patterns, making them especially suitable for traffic prediction. LSTM models can automatically learn from raw time-series data using internal memory cells and gates to capture both short-term fluctuations and long-term trends. Studies like [Zha22] have demonstrated that LSTM significantly outperforms ARIMA and SVR in terms of prediction accuracy, especially when evaluated using common metrics such as Root Mean Square Error \(RMSE\), Mean Absolute Error \(MAE\), and Mean Absolute Percentage Error \(MAPE\).)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 5679 0 R
/Next 5683 0 R
>>
endobj
5682 0 obj
<<
/Title (is not enough for the model to fully learn the traffic patterns, and, as a result, its predictions are less accurate in the first few minutes. However, after around 10 minutes of running, the model begins to recognize the pattern better, and the predicted values start to follow the real traffic. This can be observed in the graph in Figure 17, where after the initial learning period from the beggining, the two lines \(real and predicted traffic\) almost overlap. So, the delay and differences at the beginning are normal due to limited data and the model improves quickly after more data becomes available.)
