/Title (3.3 Long Short-Term Memory Model  Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) is a type of Recurrent Neural Network \(RNN\) built to handle sequential data, like time-series, speech, or text. It overcomes the vanishing gradient problem common in standard RNNs, which struggles to remember information from many steps earlier in  a sequence [Gre17].)
