/Title (3.5 GNS3  In the field of networking, the ability to test and configure network topologies as if they were physical systems, is a major advantage. It helps reduce costs and makes learning or testing much easier and more flexible. Instead of requiring physical routers, switches, and other equipment, nearly everything can be simulated on a computer. This approach is especially useful for students, engineers, and researchers who aim to build and experiment with networks without relying on a physical lab [Fon18].)
