/Title (Each metric collected is associated with a timestamp and a set of descriptive labels \(such as instance, job, or device\) to enable precise filtering and identification. The collection process is fully automated and centralized, following a pull-based model in which Prometheus initiates data retrieval from each desired endpoint. What makes Prometheus very useful is its query language, PromQL, which allows users to extract and process metrics in real time. With PromQL, we can calculate averages, detect changes over time, compare values across devices, and much more [Pro25]. This architecture allows Prometheus to maintain complete control over the frequency, scope, and organization of the monitoring process. Its ability to address targets directly via IP and port makes it well-suited for containerized environments, simulated network topologies, or distributed systems where services may run isolated and have access to the Internet [Pou24a].)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 5802 0 R
/Next 5806 0 R
>>
endobj
