/Title (Figure 3 presents the user interface of Prometheus, showing both the query entry page and the target status page. For example, a common query might be for the metric ifHCOutOctets, which shows how much outgoing network traffic was transmitted through a specific interface. The result displays a list of current values for each target \(which could be a container, a virtual machine, or another monitored device\). Each entry includes labels that help identify where the data is coming from, such as the name of the interface or the IP address of the instance. The tool also supports filtering and mathematical operations to allow more advanced analysis. This is helpful for detecting unusual patterns, slowdowns, or failures in the system. In addition to the query interface, the second panel displays the target status view, where users can see which endpoints are currently reachable, the health of each target, and when data was last successfully scraped. This allows for real-time infrastructure monitoring and quick identification of connectivity or availability issues. Together, these interface elements provide both high-level visibility and low-level control over the monitored environment.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 5804 0 R
/Next 5808 0 R
>>
