/Title (SNMP Exporter - the SNMP Exporter is designed to retrieve data from network devices that support the Simple Network Management Protocol \(SNMP\), such as routers, switches, and firewalls. SNMP works over User Datagram Protocol \(UDP\) and uses structured identifiers \(OIDs\) to expose data like interface traffic, error rates, and device status. An OID is a numerical identifier that uniquely references a specific metric or variable exposed by a device [OID25]. These identifiers follow a tree-like structure defined in standardized Management Information Bases \(MIBs\). For example, the OID .1.3.6.1.2.1.2.2.1.10 refers to ifInOctets, which represents the number of bytes received on a particular interface. Similarly, .1.3.6.1.2.1.2.2.1.16 refers to ifOutOctets, for outgoing bytes. The SNMP Exporter uses a configuration file \(.yml file\) to map human-readable metric names to these OIDs.)
/Dest [44 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 5829 0 R
/Next 5833 0 R
>>
endobj
