/Title (To ensure that the containers can communicate correctly inside the network topology, it is necessary to configure a static IP address for each one. This is done by modifying the network configuration file located at /etc/network/interfaces inside each container. The configuration  defines the IP address, subnet mask, default gateway, and DNS settings for the eth0  interface. A static IP ensures that the address remains the same, even after restarts, and it is valid  only within the GNS3 virtual network. The configuration used in each container is the same in  structure, with only the address field changing from one container to another to avoid IP  conflicts. This setting ensures reliable communication between devices.  Example of a static IP configuration for a configuration file:  # Static config for eth0  auto eth0  iface eth0 inet static  address 10.1.1.3  netmask 255.255.255.0  gateway 10.1.1.1  up echo nameserver 8.8.8.8 > /etc/resolv.conf)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 5868 0 R
/Next 5872 0 R
>>
