/Title (Accessing the metrics of each container is handled through the Cisco router, which plays a central role in connecting the internal GNS3 topology to the host machine. The router has SNMP enabled, allowing it to expose performance and traffic metrics for each of its interfaces. To enable SNMP, the following command is configured on the router: snmp-server community public RO.  In addition, the router is configured with port forwarding rules, like Network Adresse Translation \(NAT\), that redirect traffic from specific ports on its external interface to the corresponding Node Exporter ports inside each Docker container. For each container, a similar command is applied, changing only the destination IP and port to match the container's settings. For example, the command below redirects external traffic from port 9201 on the router \(with IP address 192.168.0.112\) to port 9201 on a container with IP 10.1.1.2. Similary commands are used for other containers, but their IP and ports are changed.)
/Dest [48 0 R /Fit]
